_Content updated: 2 October 2026. Provider-source research: 10 September 2026._

This guide compares 12 UK GEO providers for 2026 using their published services, case studies, methodology and pricing. **Commercial disclosure:** I own Sunny Patel SEO and benefit if readers hire my practice. Its listing is an owned-service profile, shown first and labelled separately; that placement is not an independent ranking. No other provider paid for inclusion, and I have no commercial relationship with the other providers listed. The review is not an exhaustive market survey or a controlled comparison of results.

GEO (Generative Engine Optimisation) is the practice of getting a brand cited across generative AI systems: Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Copilot. Published service descriptions and measured AI outcomes are different evidence. This guide identifies the evidence described for each provider without assuming that an unpublished result does not exist. It is the GEO sibling to my [best AEO agencies](/blog/best-aeo-agencies/) review, and the next section explains how the two terms differ.

**Directory inclusion:** providers with a published GEO or AI-search offer, public methodology or work examples, and service information useful to UK buyers. The review records whether AI-specific evidence is published; a citation or conversion was not a requirement that every listed provider met. These are inclusion checks, not competitive scoring criteria.

---

## What is GEO (and how it differs from AEO and SEO)

**GEO (Generative Engine Optimisation)** is the practice of earning citations across generative AI systems, including Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Copilot. The goal is to be the source a generative engine names when it composes an answer. **AEO (Answer Engine Optimisation)** is the narrower version focused on direct answers from assistants and answer engines. **SEO** earns traditional blue-link rankings.

GEO, AEO and SEO can share technical, editorial and entity work, but an improvement in one channel does not establish a result in another. For Google AI Overviews and AI Mode, [Google says existing SEO practices remain relevant](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features): pages must be indexed and eligible for a Search snippet, and no special AI schema is required. That is eligibility guidance for Google, not a description of how every assistant selects citations. Ask a GEO provider which platforms it tests and which outcomes its work has actually produced.

For the underlying mechanics, see [what is LLM optimisation](/blog/what-is-llm-optimisation/) and [how to optimise content for AI search](/blog/optimise-content-for-ai-search/).

Whether you call them GEO companies, GEO SEO agencies, or a generative engine optimisation agency, the same evidence bar applies: a documented citation, over a services page claim.

---

Similarweb reported **357%** year-on-year growth in AI referral traffic to the top 1,000 websites in June 2025. That is a sampled referral trend, not proof of lost traffic caused by the absence of a brand citation. Seer separately observed lower organic CTR in its tracked AI Overview query cohort from June 2024 to September 2025; those comparisons do not isolate causation. The [AI search statistics](/blog/ai-search-statistics/) page distinguishes the populations, dates and outcomes.

