## Hiring a GEO specialist vs a GEO agency

A GEO specialist, typically a sole consultant or a two-to-three-person team, works directly on your account, understands your entity and content set in detail, and usually costs less than a full agency retainer. The trade-off is capacity: a specialist cannot run a large content programme or a big digital PR campaign alongside GEO work. Sunny Patel SEO on this list is a specialist example, and says so plainly in its own considerations.

A GEO agency, from a boutique like Semetrical or Screaming Frog through to a full-service shop like Rise at Seven or Impression Digital, brings more people and more channels: content teams, digital PR, technical SEO, and in some cases paid media, all under one contract. That suits a brand that wants generative-engine work coordinated alongside a bigger organic or paid programme, and can absorb the higher retainer that comes with it.

Neither model is inherently better. Ask any provider, specialist or agency, for a documented AI citation before signing; capacity and price differ, but the evidence bar for genuine GEO capability should not.

